updater_backup/
# Every other git-ignored local state file (tests/test_supply_chain_qa.py keeps
# this list a superset of .gitignore): the team change queue, Posture plus
# settings, self-healing state and the last-good / damaged copies it keeps of
# the stores above (a tenant_profiles.json.last-good holds what
# tenant_profiles.json holds), and atomic-write temporaries.
change_requests.json
change_requests.json.lock
.change_requests.*.tmp
.workspace_notes.*.tmp
posture_settings.json
update_notify.json
plugins.json
sync_jobs.json
sync_jobs.json.lock
.sync_jobs.*.tmp
config_backups/
self_heal.json
**/*.last-good
**/*.corrupt-*
.selfheal-*.tmp
# Temporary copies a crash can leave mid-write (they may hold the UI token or a
# remembered secret): never in the image.
.profiles-*
.ui_token_*
.fingerprint-*
.deployments-*
.posture-*
.update-notify-*
.plugins-*
# Store encryption (store_crypto.py): the key file, the one-time migration's
# journal and its plaintext safety backup, their atomic-write temporaries, and
# the lock that lets one process at a time change the key.
# The key beside the data must never be committed or baked into an image.
store_keys.json
.store_keys.json.*.tmp
store_encryption_migration.json
.store_encryption_migration.json.*.tmp
store-encryption-backup/
.store_crypto.lock
# Editor, OS and build leftovers.
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

agent-workspace/output/
